  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The narrative centers on the Skaergaard project’s transition from a geological concept to a formal U.S.-compliant resource, with a material upgrade in indicated contained metal and grade positioning it as a regulatory asset. The wider backdrop is a Western push to build a critical-minerals supply chain outside China, lending geopolitical tailwinds to Greenland’s resource potential. The company is advancing a “North Atlantic Critical Metals Corridor” linking Greenland resources to allied downstream processing. Note: all commentary is drawn from company-issued promotional releases, so the bullish framing lacks independent verification.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is signaling conviction through a large open-market insider purchase by the CFO, raising his ownership materially. Strategically, the company has executed a share-exchange with AnorTech and attracted an investment from SRX Global, actions that support the corridor vision and suggest intent to convert resources into a broader supply-chain play. These moves present a narrative of aligned insider interests and deliberate partnership-building, though the information is sourced solely from company announcements.",
