        "snippet": "A Greenland Deposit Just Got Its First U.S.-Compliant Resource Report, and the Indicated Grade Jumped 36% Accessibility Statement Skip Navigation\n\nIssued on behalf of Greenland Mines Ltd.\n\nGreenland Mines Ltd. (NASDAQ: GRML) reported that independent consultant SLR Consulting (Canada) Ltd. has completed the first SEC S-K 1300-compliant Technical Report Summary for its Skaergaard project in southeast Greenland, with an updated Mineral Resource Estimate effective July 3, 2026 that lifts indicated contained palladium-equivalent metal 31% to 15.0 million ounces and indicated grade 36% to 3.04 g/t PdEq versus the project's 2022 estimate.\n\nLOS ANGELES, July 17, 2026 /CNW/ -- Equity Insider News Commentary, There is a specific moment in a mining project's life when it stops being a geological idea and starts being a regulatory asset. It happens when an independent firm signs its name to a resource statement prepared under the disclosure standard that governs the exchange the company trades on",
